---
import Footer from '../../components/parts/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/parts/Header.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, BUSINESS } from '../../lib/site';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const canonical = absoluteUrl('/en/privacy-policy');
const h2 = 'mb-4 font-segmentA text-4xl uppercase tracking-wide font-bold text-primary md:text-5xl';
const link = 'text-primary underline';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Benito Gonzalez Sax"
  description="Privacy policy for Benito Gonzalez Sax: quote requests from the website and from Facebook and Instagram lead ad forms, CRM, your rights and data deletion."
  lang="en"
  canonical={canonical}
  alternates={[
    { hreflang: 'en', href: canonical },
    { hreflang: 'es', href: absoluteUrl('/politica-de-privacidad') },
    { hreflang: 'x-default', href: absoluteUrl('/') },
  ]}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="pb-16 pt-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4">
      <h1 class="mb-4 font-segmentA text-6xl uppercase tracking-wide font-bold text-primary md:text-8xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-gray-700">
        <p>
          This policy explains how we process the personal data you provide through this website, through the forms in our Facebook and
          Instagram ads and through direct contact channels, in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018
          on the Protection of Personal Data and Guarantee of Digital Rights (LOPDGDD).
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>1. Data controller</h2>
          <p>
            The data controller is <strong>{BUSINESS.legalName}</strong>, operating commercially as <strong>{BUSINESS.name}</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Contact email: <a href={BUSINESS.emailHref} class={link}>{BUSINESS.email}</a><br />
            Phone: <a href={BUSINESS.phoneHref} class={link}>{BUSINESS.phone}</a><br />
            Professional address: {BUSINESS.addressLocality}, {BUSINESS.addressRegion}, Spain.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>2. Data collected and its source</h2>
          <p>We only request the data needed to answer information and quote requests. It may come from:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              <strong>This website's contact form:</strong> name, email, phone number, event date, event city or venue, requested service type and
              message. The form opens your email or WhatsApp app, and the data only reaches us if you send the message.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Meta lead ad forms (Facebook and Instagram):</strong> the same data you submit in the ad form (name, email, phone number,
              event date, event city or venue, service type and, where applicable, a message). Meta may pre-fill some fields with information from
              your profile, which you can review and edit before submitting. Along with your answers we receive technical submission data: date and
              time, ad, campaign and form identifiers, and the source platform.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Direct contact</strong> by email, phone or WhatsApp: the data you choose to share in the conversation.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Browsing:</strong> technical and analytics data about website usage (pages visited, device, approximate location).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">We do not request special categories of data (health, beliefs, etc.).</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>3. Purpose of processing</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>Reply to quote requests and enquiries about weddings and events.</li>
            <li>
              Record requests received through the website or through Meta lead ad forms in our customer relationship management tool (CRM) to
              organise and follow up on your enquiry: availability, quote and booking.
            </li>
            <li>Manage follow-up communication by email, phone or WhatsApp.</li>
            <li>Provide the service and handle invoicing if you book it.</li>
            <li>Measure website usage and improve its performance.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Your data is only used to handle your request and the resulting commercial relationship. We will not send you marketing communications
            unrelated to your request without your prior consent, and we do not make automated decisions or create profiles that produce legal
            effects concerning you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>4. Legal basis</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              <strong>Pre-contractual steps taken at your request</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR): replying to your information or quote request,
              whether sent from the website, a Meta lead ad form or a direct channel, and recording it in the CRM for follow-up.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Performance of a contract</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR): providing the booked service.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR): keeping tax and accounting records.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR): website analytics and, where applicable, marketing communications. You may withdraw it at
              any time without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>5. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            Data from requests that do not lead to a booking is kept for as long as needed to handle the enquiry and its commercial follow-up, and is
            deleted once it is no longer needed or when you ask us to. If you book the service, data is kept for the duration of the contractual
            relationship and afterwards for the periods required by tax and commercial law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>6. Recipients and providers</h2>
          <p>
            Personal data is not sold, rented or disclosed to third parties for their own purposes. Only the providers needed to deliver the service
            have access to it, as data processors or within the scope of their own services:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              <strong>Meta Platforms Ireland Limited</strong> (Facebook, Instagram) as the ads and lead form platform, and
              <strong> WhatsApp Ireland Limited</strong> if you contact us via WhatsApp. Meta's processing of your account data is governed by its own
              <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class={link}>privacy policy</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Meta for Developers app:</strong> we use our own app registered on Meta for Developers solely to automatically receive the data
              submitted through our ad forms and record it in our CRM. This app does not access any other data from your Facebook or Instagram
              account (contacts, posts, messages, etc.). Data obtained through Meta is not sold, is not shared with third parties for their own
              purposes and is only used for the purposes described in this policy.
            </li>
            <li>The provider of the customer relationship management tool (CRM), which stores requests on the controller's behalf.</li>
            <li>Google (Firebase Hosting and Google Analytics) for website hosting and measurement, and the email provider.</li>
            <li>Public authorities, courts and tribunals where there is a legal obligation.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>7. International transfers</h2>
          <p>
            Some providers (such as Meta or Google) may process data outside the European Economic Area. In those cases, transfers rely on a European
            Commission adequacy decision, such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, or on standard contractual clauses approved by the European
            Commission.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>8. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You may exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing and portability, and withdraw your
            consent, by emailing <a href={BUSINESS.emailHref} class={link}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>. We will reply within one month at the latest. If we
            have reasonable doubts about your identity, we may ask for additional information to confirm it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            If you believe the processing does not comply with the applicable regulations, you may lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection
            Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class={link}>www.aepd.es</a>).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="data-deletion" class="scroll-mt-32">
          <h2 class={h2}>9. How to request deletion of your data</h2>
          <p>
            If you sent us your data through this website, a Facebook or Instagram lead ad form or any other channel, you can ask us to delete it at
            any time:
          </p>
          <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              Email <a href={BUSINESS.emailHref} class={link}>{BUSINESS.email}</a> with the subject "Delete my data".
            </li>
            <li>Include the name, email or phone number you used to send the request.</li>
            <li>
              We will delete your data from the CRM, email and messaging channels within one month at the latest and confirm it by email, except for
              data we must keep by law, which will remain blocked only for the required period.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-4">
            This request covers the data we hold. Data that Meta keeps in your Facebook or Instagram account is managed from your account's privacy
            settings on those platforms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>10. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data against unauthorised access, loss or alteration. Access to
            requests is limited to the data controller.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>11. Minors</h2>
          <p>
            Our services are aimed at adults. We do not knowingly collect data from children under 14; if we find that we have received such data, we
            will delete it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            This privacy policy may be updated to reflect legal, technical or operational changes. The version published on this page, with its last
            updated date, is always the one in force.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
